§ `Codex Insurance Limited — Daily Hospital Income Policy`

-- Encoding of fixtures/chubb-policy.txt.
--
-- Per the task brief, every date/time referenced by a query -- other than the
-- claimant's age -- is given as a NUMBER of months elapsed since the policy's
-- effective date, so no absolute DATE arithmetic is needed anywhere below.
--
-- Per the task brief, §1.1 conditions 1 ("this agreement is signed") and 2
-- ("the applicable premium ... has been paid") are assumed always satisfied,
-- as is §4.5's premium-timing requirement; none of the three is modelled.
-- §2.3's requirement that "a claim must be made to the Company setting out
-- the basis for making the claim" is a filing/procedural requirement, not a
-- substantive coverage condition: it is satisfied whenever the substantive
-- conditions below hold, so it is not modelled as a separate fact.
-- §4.2 (arbitration), §4.3 (New York law) and §4.4 (US currency) govern
-- dispute resolution and payment mechanics, not whether a claim is covered,
-- and are likewise not modelled.

§§ `Ontology`

DECLARE `Excluded Activity` IS ONE OF
    Skydiving
    `Military Service`
    `Firefighter Service`
    `Police Service`

-- `Intentional Self Inflicted Injury` is a deliberate act by the claimant --
-- see NOTES.md for why this is treated as neither a sickness nor an
-- accidental injury under §2.1.
DECLARE `Cause Of Hospitalization` IS ONE OF
    Sickness
    `Accidental Injury`
    `Intentional Self Inflicted Injury`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `cause of hospitalization`                                          IS A `Cause Of Hospitalization`
    `excluded activity`                                                 IS A MAYBE `Excluded Activity`
    `age at hospitalization`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `hospital located in the United States`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `days confined in hospital`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `hospitalization months after the effective date`                   IS A NUMBER
    `wellness visit occurred months after the effective date`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `wellness visit confirmation given months after the effective date` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `fraud misrepresentation or material withholding of information`    IS A BOOLEAN

§ `1. POLICY IN EFFECT AND CONDITIONS`

§§ `1.3 — the wellness-visit condition`

-- "... written confirmation ... of a wellness visit ... occurring no later
--  than the 6th month anniversary of the effective date of this policy."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit occurred in time` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit occurred months after the effective date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m THEN m AT MOST 6

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date of this
--  policy, you will supply us with written confirmation ..."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit confirmation given in time` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit confirmation given months after the effective date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m THEN m AT MOST 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim MEANS
    `wellness visit occurred in time` claim
    AND `wellness visit confirmation given in time` claim

-- "is still pending": as of the hospitalization for which the claim is made,
-- the 7th-month deadline for satisfying §1.3 has not yet arrived.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 still pending` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization months after the effective date` AT MOST 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 met` claim MEANS
    `condition 1.3 still pending` claim
    OR `condition 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim

§§ `4.6 — policy term (referenced by 1.2's automatic cancelation at term end)`

-- "will last for a period of one year from that date [the effective date]"
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`within the one-year policy term` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization months after the effective date` AT MOST 12

§§ `1.2 — cancelation`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
    claim's `fraud misrepresentation or material withholding of information`
    OR NOT `condition 1.3 met` claim
    OR NOT `within the one-year policy term` claim

§§ `1.1 — policy in effect`

-- Conditions 1 and 2 (signed; premium paid) are assumed satisfied -- see the
-- file header. Condition 3 ("the condition set out in Section 1.3 is still
-- pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion") is folded into
-- `policy canceled` above; condition 4 is "the policy has not been canceled".
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at the hospitalization` claim MEANS
    NOT `policy canceled` claim

§ `2. BENEFITS`

-- "If you have been confined in a hospital as a result of sickness or
--  accidental Injury, we will pay you the Daily Hospital Income Benefit."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `cause of hospitalization`
    WHEN Sickness THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental Injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Intentional Self Inflicted Injury` THEN FALSE

-- "The Daily Hospital Income Benefit will only be payable for each (24 hour)
--  day of continuous confinement in a hospital in the United States ... and
--  for a period not exceeding three hundred and sixty-five (365) days ..."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`benefit payable under section 2.2` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospital located in the United States`
    AND claim's `days confined in hospital` AT MOST 365

§ `3. GENERAL EXCLUSIONS`

-- "... any event causing sickness or accidental injury arising directly or
--  indirectly out of: Skydiving; Service in the military; Service as a fire
--  fighter; Service in the police." This requires the hospitalization to
-- have arisen from engaging in the activity, not merely that the claimant
-- holds that occupation at the time -- see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`activity exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `excluded activity`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST activity THEN TRUE

-- "If your age at the time of the hospitalization is equal to or greater
--  than 80 years of age."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`age exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a general exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    `activity exclusion applies` claim
    OR `age exclusion applies` claim

§ `Coverage decision`

-- §2.3's filing requirement ("a claim must be made ... setting out the basis
-- for making the claim and for there being no exclusion or cancellation") is
-- satisfied exactly when the substantive conditions below hold; see the file
-- header note.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered` claim MEANS
    `policy in effect at the hospitalization` claim
    AND `hospitalization is sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND `benefit payable under section 2.2` claim
    AND NOT `a general exclusion applies` claim
